73:.agent-progress/
533:- **Redraw harness**: without a TTY, v2 sends its own `WindowSizeMsg` built from 0×0, which shrinks the view to 489 bytes. Fixed in `e44dcb0`, see D114.
570:**D114 — DEVDESK-201: the redraw cost of Bubble Tea v2 against v1 (`TestMeasureRedrawCost`). Measured; the threshold is +25 %; the verdict is within it.** **Plane:** DEVDESK-201 (G2), analysis DEVDESK-201 (perf)
587:- **`View()` cost (D114 perf analysis, DEVDESK-201).** Isolated benchmark, `GOMAXPROCS=1`, 7 interleaved runs: v1 Ascii 288 µs, v1 TrueColor 683 µs, v2 868 µs. Real surcharge against v1 TrueColor: **+27 %**. The "×2.5–3" of the first measure is mostly an artefact: 12 to 60 cold calls, no warm-up. In-program: about 1.5 ms (v1 TrueColor) against about 2.0 ms cold (v2).
610:`7091e78` imports and `go.mod` (A1) → `a74a262` theme `color.Color` and hex validation (A2) → `0692c35` keys, `KeyPressMsg`, `keymap.Space = "space"` (B) → `ba1d938` Bubbles and Lip Gloss APIs (D1) → `495409b` ntcharts v2 and module tidy (E) → `89f32a3` `Render` and `View() tea.View`, router owns `AltScreen` (C) → `dab9d28` fix: nil `confirmModal` guard removed from the setup wizard render → `ad0900d` Rule 135 (B2, D113) → `0618f37` viewport KeyMap guard (D2) → `6aa865d` paste routed to the focused field (D3) → `e65ab2f` colour profile from Bubble Tea, `termenv` removed (F) → `103e80b` fix: paste into every focused field of the forge explorer → `1958602` chore: import groups → `e44dcb0` redraw measure repaired (D114).
629:> **Correction (2026-11-10, DEVDESK-201, D114 analysis).** (a) The v1 base of this table ran with the Ascii profile, not forced TrueColor: `go test` has no TTY, and Lip Gloss v1 converted no colour. Forced TrueColor on v1 gives 5945 bytes per redraw (20 rows) and about 1.5 ms of `View()` in-program; v2 gives 863 bytes: −85 % against v1 TrueColor (−70 % against the Ascii base). (b) The "×2.5–3" `View()` ratio of this entry is mostly a cold-call artefact (12 to 60 calls). Isolated benchmark, `GOMAXPROCS=1`: v1 Ascii 288 µs, v1 TrueColor 683 µs, v2 868 µs: a real +27 % against TrueColor. (c) The rest is in `x/ansi` (see D114). The figures above are not rewritten.
internal/app/redraw_measure_test.go
	return v
}

// Render renders the interface: header, title line, viewport, footer (Rule 124).
// An open overlay replaces the whole thing.
func (a *App) Render() string {
	if overlay := a.activeOverlay(); overlay != "" {
		return lipgloss.Place(a.width, a.height, lipgloss.Center, lipgloss.Center, overlay,
			lipgloss.WithWhitespaceStyle(lipgloss.NewStyle().Background(theme.ColorBackground)))
	}

	header := a.renderHeader() + "\n" + a.renderTitleLine()
	// The footer is rendered first: whether a bar opens it decides how the
	// viewport closes its bottom edge.
	footer := a.renderViewFooter()
	barBelow := !a.frameless() && components.OpensWithBarFrame(footer)
	case a.switchingTo != "":
		return a.renderContextSwitchingOverlay()
	case a.showHelp:
		return a.renderHelpOverlay()
	case a.showContextList:
		return a.renderContextListOverlay()
	}
	return ""
}

// renderBody fills the viewport with the active view's content, padded to the
// full inner width so no line shows the terminal's own background (Rule 115).
// barBelow is true when the footer opens with a components.BarFrame: the
// viewport's bottom corners then become T-junctions (Rule 136).
func (a *App) renderBody(barBelow bool) string {
	content := "View not found: " + string(a.currentView)

